\setaudiodev sets the audio device used by Python (pyo),
for both input and output.
It takes one argument, the ID of the device, as printed
by \listaudiodev:

\listaudiodev
\setaudiodev 2

If the ID is negative or not in the list, you will get
an error.
Like all audio settings, it must be called before \python
is called for the first time, otherwise it has no effect.
If no device is set, the system's default one is used.

To set the input or output device separately, use
\setinaudiodev or \setoutaudiodev.
